# Loaded by the shared vitest config only when the run is SEQUENTIAL (fileParallelism: false).
# It is that run's declaration that it may DESTROY the test database.
#
# schemaSynchronizer.test.ts regenerates the schema from scratch — cleanDatabase() drops every table,
# then the sample graph is reloaded. Sequentially that is invisible: the gap falls between files. Run
# file-by-file (the Test Explorer, or plain `--test`, which is parallel), it lands in the MIDDLE of
# ~95 other files querying the same database, and they fail with "relation ... does not exist".
#
# So the destructive suite is opt-in rather than opt-out: it runs where it is safe, and skips with a
# reason everywhere else. A checked-in env file rather than a shell prefix because `VAR=1 cmd` is not
# portable to Windows, where these scripts also run.
ALTEA_TEST_DESTRUCTIVE=1
